 "_doc": "R29 / A4: which cluster unit the CIs of Tabs. S3 (supp_e54a), S6 (supp_e60), S20 (supp_judge) use, and recomputation\nwith image / scene clustering where several analysed units share an image or scene.\n\nS3  rigor_e54.share_boot on bundle/e54_decomp.json _records. Per-model rows: clusters = Exp-45 'cl' (cue set: the 400\n    twin-pair scenes, 4 prompts each; twins: the 200 scenes, both twin images and both phrasings; Syn. Depth 431: the\n    image), strata = model x set. Pooled 'All seven' row: same clusters, strata = model x set, i.e. the same scene is\n    resampled independently for each of the 7 models. Recomputed here: (a) as published; (b) scene clusters shared across\n    models (strata = set; one draw of a scene takes its D+C- records of all 7 models); (c) item level (no clustering).\nS6  rigor_e60.Boot: clusters = CV-Bench item ('group' = idx); one draw is shared by all models and contexts. Checked\n    here: CV-Bench source photo (test.json source_filename) of the 151 kept items.\nS20 make_supp_tables.judge_table: Wilson intervals on the judged first claims (one claim per Synthetic Depth item);\n    consensus from bundle/judge2.json (Wilson); Rule (all) from bundle/claim_strat.json (bootstrap over item uids).\n    Checked here: items per image, and the post-'unclear' denominators behind each judged rate.\n-> outputs/bundle/r29_cluster_check.json, outputs/bundle/rigor_r29_cluster_check.txt\nUsage: python r29_cluster_check.py\n",
